{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792247974,"nonce":"dxzffGgbhyOkRjk/ATEBpwIqing=","title":"State::set leaves an effect's writes queued","message":"`Signal::set` drains `DEFERRED_WRITES` after notifying; `State::set`, `set_rebuild`, `update` and `update_rebuild` did not. Effects run while the graph is held, so a signal an effect writes is deferred, and after a `State` write nothing applied it until some unrelated `Signal::set` happened to drain the queue.\n\nFound migrating cn number_input: an effect on its `State\u003cf64\u003e` writes the formatted value into the field and bumps the field's revision; the write sat in the queue and the field never showed the step.\n\nFix: the four `State` mutators drain deferred writes after their notifications, as `Signal::set` does. Test: `reactive::tests::a_write_an_effect_makes_lands_when_state_set_returns`, which fails without the drain.","files":null}]}